1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
"A Winter Sun Wakes the Wind in Spring Hills' Dream Extra Episode"

2
00:00:11,093 --> 00:00:15,593
(Episode 3: Outside of Time)

3
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:23,480
Start talking.

4
00:00:24,359 --> 00:00:25,559
Where did you come from?

5
00:00:26,079 --> 00:00:27,280
I said spill it!

6
00:00:28,399 --> 00:00:29,920
Where did you dig up this body double?

7
00:00:30,079 --> 00:00:32,399
And you're trying to fool me with
sci-fi nonsense about time travel?

8
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:33,959
You saw the footage of the jump yourself.

9
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:35,040
I couldn't have faked that.

10
00:00:35,079 --> 00:00:36,560
Seeing isn't always believing.

11
00:00:36,920 --> 00:00:37,920
Tell the truth.

12
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:41,678
What is this place...?

13
00:00:41,679 --> 00:00:42,679
Shut up.

14
00:00:43,079 --> 00:00:44,359
Nobody asked you.

15
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:47,735
If you're hiring a double, at least
pick someone who acts like me.

16
00:00:47,759 --> 00:00:49,719
Did I really sound that
squeaky when I was young?

17
00:00:50,759 --> 00:00:51,879
I wouldn't know.

18
00:00:51,880 --> 00:00:52,880
How should I know?

19
00:00:54,320 --> 00:00:55,320
Feng Qinglang.

20
00:00:56,079 --> 00:00:56,679
Yeah?

21
00:00:56,679 --> 00:00:57,679
Hmm?

22
00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:02,280
Stop messing around. Let
me ask him two questions.

23
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:06,400
Where were you this
morning? What were you doing?

24
00:01:07,159 --> 00:01:08,920
I was on set shooting.

25
00:01:11,159 --> 00:01:12,159
Had you been drinking?

26
00:01:12,319 --> 00:01:13,319
Huh?

27
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:17,840
Do you realize you traveled through time?

28
00:01:18,760 --> 00:01:20,920
No leading questions!

29
00:01:22,959 --> 00:01:25,000
You traveled through time, get it?

30
00:01:25,799 --> 00:01:27,920
From twenty-one to thirty-five.

31
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:29,560
Yeah.

32
00:01:30,079 --> 00:01:31,319
Drop the act and talk normally.

33
00:01:32,959 --> 00:01:33,959
Alright.

34
00:01:55,959 --> 00:01:57,679
Plotting how to send me back...

35
00:01:57,703 --> 00:01:59,023
And keeping him here instead, right?

36
00:02:00,159 --> 00:02:02,959
At twenty-one, he's five
years younger than you.

37
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:04,799
Quite a match, isn't he?

38
00:02:05,760 --> 00:02:08,040
I've never seen anyone get
jealous of their younger self.

39
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:15,199
Let him stay then.

40
00:02:21,919 --> 00:02:25,399
If he goes back, he's bound to fall for that
jerk Shi Yuhao again. Would you like that?

41
00:02:27,719 --> 00:02:29,319
If he stays and falls for you,

42
00:02:29,479 --> 00:02:30,680
I'd like that even less.

43
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:33,640
Are we sending him back or not?

44
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:36,800
Fine! Send him back, send him back!

45
00:03:00,319 --> 00:03:01,799
Can I stay?

46
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:02,800
No.

47
00:03:04,960 --> 00:03:06,520
How can you be so cold-hearted?

48
00:03:07,599 --> 00:03:09,656
If I weren't ruthless, how
else could I dump scumbags?

49
00:03:09,680 --> 00:03:11,120
Listen to me, Feng Qinglang.

50
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:13,000
Once you go back, focus on your work.

51
00:03:13,319 --> 00:03:14,800
Act in roles. Win awards.

52
00:03:15,199 --> 00:03:16,159
No dating.

53
00:03:16,159 --> 00:03:17,159
No chasing PR scandals.

54
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:20,120
And definitely no falling
for a costar on every shoot.

55
00:03:20,319 --> 00:03:22,199
Don't be boy-crazy.

56
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:24,319
Keep your nose clean.

57
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:27,120
And at twenty-nine, wait for
your husband to come find you.

58
00:03:28,159 --> 00:03:29,159
Hmph.

59
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:37,360
Go.

60
00:04:43,399 --> 00:04:45,360
All right, that looks good, crane up.

61
00:04:51,680 --> 00:04:53,320
Why does this makeup
make them look so old?

62
00:04:54,360 --> 00:04:55,399
Director, I'm here!

63
00:04:56,959 --> 00:04:57,959
When time is it?

64
00:04:59,199 --> 00:05:00,199
Uh...

65
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:03,159
August 2028.

66
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:05,040
I know that! I asked
what time it is right now.

67
00:05:05,079 --> 00:05:06,600
Let's soften the light on you a bit.

68
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:08,800
Shift the light over this way.

69
00:05:14,399 --> 00:05:17,680
Pick up, pick up, pick up!

70
00:05:19,959 --> 00:05:21,855
Stand-in, you're in the shot!
Step off set to make your call!

71
00:05:21,879 --> 00:05:23,319
Tian, where are you? Tian!

72
00:05:23,879 --> 00:05:24,600
Hey, Tian!

73
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:25,600
Where are you?

74
00:05:27,279 --> 00:05:28,720
Tian! Tian!

75
00:05:28,879 --> 00:05:30,279
What are you screeching for?

76
00:05:30,560 --> 00:05:31,519
Where on earth are you?

77
00:05:31,520 --> 00:05:32,720
Just tell me!

78
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:35,120
Why should I tell you?

79
00:05:37,519 --> 00:05:39,279
You're on a date with Chen Zhu, aren't you?

80
00:05:39,399 --> 00:05:40,720
If you don't tell me,

81
00:05:40,879 --> 00:05:42,600
I'll tell Mom you're dating someone!

82
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:45,398
Feng Qinglang, are you
done? I'm hanging up.

83
00:05:45,399 --> 00:05:46,399
Wait!

84
00:05:46,519 --> 00:05:47,319
Ah!

85
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:48,160
Bro?

86
00:05:48,360 --> 00:05:49,160
Ah!

87
00:05:49,199 --> 00:05:49,879
Ouch!

88
00:05:49,879 --> 00:05:50,519
Bro!

89
00:05:50,519 --> 00:05:51,079
Ah!

90
00:05:51,080 --> 00:05:52,319
Are you blind?

91
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:55,600
Bro?

92
00:05:55,920 --> 00:05:56,920
Are you okay?

93
00:05:57,319 --> 00:05:59,079
I can't move!

94
00:05:59,319 --> 00:06:00,879
Bro, my leg is broken!

95
00:06:01,279 --> 00:06:02,759
Aren't you on set?

96
00:06:04,279 --> 00:06:05,279
Yeah, right!

97
00:06:05,720 --> 00:06:08,720
A production car hit me on set!

98
00:06:09,279 --> 00:06:11,719
Director, that veteran stand-in
is lying through his teeth.

99
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:13,719
He claims one of our
crew cars ran him over.

100
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:14,799
He's on the phone calling his people!

101
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:16,278
Hurry over and see your brother!

102
00:06:16,279 --> 00:06:18,000
Before it's too late!

103
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:19,560
His acting is terrible. Recast him.

104
00:06:20,519 --> 00:06:23,279
Feng Qinglang, you'd better
actually have been hit by a car.

105
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:25,200
Because if you're faking, you're dead.

106
00:06:26,879 --> 00:06:27,879
Tian!

107
00:06:28,160 --> 00:06:28,959
Ah!

108
00:06:29,120 --> 00:06:30,120
All right, all right!

109
00:06:30,279 --> 00:06:31,279
Stop screaming bloody murder.

110
00:06:31,279 --> 00:06:31,879
Send the address.

111
00:06:31,879 --> 00:06:32,720
No need to send it.

112
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:33,879
Don't hang up.

113
00:06:33,959 --> 00:06:35,278
Hail a cab and hand
the phone to the driver.

114
00:06:35,279 --> 00:06:36,399
I'll give him directions.

115
00:06:36,600 --> 00:06:38,518
I need you to stay on the line.

116
00:06:38,519 --> 00:06:41,278
I don't want to spend my final
moments without hearing your voice.

117
00:06:41,279 --> 00:06:42,279
Tian...

118
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:43,879
You lunatic.

119
00:06:47,879 --> 00:06:49,479
You're out of the cab? Good.

120
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:51,479
Follow the small lane
from where you got off,

121
00:06:51,480 --> 00:06:52,480
past the white wall.

122
00:06:52,519 --> 00:06:53,279
Walk along it,

123
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:56,160
then turn right and you'll see me, okay?

124
00:06:56,360 --> 00:06:57,560
Yeah, just keep walking.

125
00:06:57,920 --> 00:06:59,720
Don't hang up, bro...

126
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:02,879
I'm scared you won't make
it to see me one last time.

127
00:07:03,199 --> 00:07:04,480
If I can't hear your voice...

128
00:07:04,519 --> 00:07:06,278
I'll be so terrified.

129
00:07:06,279 --> 00:07:07,318
My leg hurts so bad!

130
00:07:07,319 --> 00:07:08,079
My leg is broken!

131
00:07:08,080 --> 00:07:09,959
It really is broken, I swear—.

132
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:11,000
Feng Qinglang!

133
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:12,879
You played me again!

134
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:15,399
Tian!

135
00:07:15,480 --> 00:07:16,758
What kind of stunt are you
pulling in the middle of the night?

136
00:07:16,759 --> 00:07:18,279
Why did you trick me into coming here?

137
00:07:18,720 --> 00:07:21,359
To stop you from dating, obviously!

138
00:07:21,360 --> 00:07:22,360
Mind your own business!

139
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:24,480
If I don't look out for you, who will?

140
00:07:24,519 --> 00:07:26,679
Come on, your brother is
taking you out for good food.

141
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:29,920
Just because you're single
doesn't mean you can ruin my life!

142
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:31,360
Who says I can't find someone?

143
00:07:31,560 --> 00:07:33,120
I just don't want to.

144
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,920
Feng Qinglang, this is
what you brought me to eat?

145
00:07:41,279 --> 00:07:42,560
You conned me again!

146
00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:46,079
Don't be picky. Be glad you're getting fed.

147
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:51,920
Oh, by the way,

148
00:07:52,120 --> 00:07:53,719
send Chen Zhu a text.

149
00:07:53,720 --> 00:07:54,879
See if he's all right.

150
00:07:55,079 --> 00:07:56,360
I almost forgot!

151
00:07:57,279 --> 00:07:59,079
You completely ruined my date.

152
00:08:04,399 --> 00:08:06,079
He didn't get into a car accident, did he?

153
00:08:07,399 --> 00:08:10,120
You think everyone's a
drama queen like you?

154
00:08:13,372 --> 00:08:16,352
[Previous messages: Where
did you go? I'm waiting for you.]

155
00:08:16,466 --> 00:08:19,432
[Something came up
today, let's take a rain check]

156
00:09:19,720 --> 00:09:20,919
Can it really be changed?

157
00:09:24,799 --> 00:09:26,200
In this timeline, I don't know.

158
00:09:26,799 --> 00:09:28,239
In that timeline, it definitely can.

159
00:09:38,399 --> 00:09:40,120
Everyone's destiny will change.

160
00:09:43,799 --> 00:09:45,080
Chen Zhu won't get into a crash,

161
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:49,559
Wenshu will never meet Qingtian,

162
00:09:52,799 --> 00:09:53,918
and you and I won't...

163
00:09:53,919 --> 00:09:54,919
No.

164
00:09:56,480 --> 00:09:58,120
You and I exist beyond time.

165
00:10:02,799 --> 00:10:04,056
No matter which timeline we're in,

166
00:10:04,080 --> 00:10:05,320
we will always find each other.

167
00:10:49,399 --> 00:10:51,879
Bro, I found the Ghost Flower!

168
00:10:59,440 --> 00:11:00,679
Hey, don't run!

169
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:02,560
The path is slippery this morning.

170
00:11:22,799 --> 00:11:23,799
How's it look?

171
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:25,960
Take a look.

172
00:11:26,440 --> 00:11:27,440
What's the deal with you two?

173
00:11:27,441 --> 00:11:29,679
All morning and that's all
you picked? Look at mine.

174
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:34,056
We're foraging for termite mushrooms.

175
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:35,199
What you have grows everywhere.

176
00:11:35,200 --> 00:11:36,200
How can you even compare?

177
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:42,480
Why are you two tied together?

178
00:11:43,480 --> 00:11:44,399
The pup wouldn't behave.

179
00:11:44,399 --> 00:11:45,279
Worried he'd wander off.

180
00:11:45,280 --> 00:11:46,599
You're taking forever!
I'm heading back first.

181
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:47,600
Hey.

182
00:12:22,240 --> 00:12:23,399
Hungry?

183
00:12:51,440 --> 00:12:52,600
I miss my brother.

184
00:12:56,559 --> 00:12:57,960
I saw him.

185
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:01,360
I saw him, too.

186
00:13:03,639 --> 00:13:04,639
Really?

187
00:13:09,440 --> 00:13:10,879
It wasn't my imagination.

188
00:13:13,840 --> 00:13:15,200
He's been in the forest all along.

189
00:13:18,960 --> 00:13:22,399
You're bluffing. Tell me
then, what did he say to me?

190
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:24,480
He said he found the Ghost Flower,

191
00:13:24,559 --> 00:13:25,798
and complained that we
were walking too slowly.

192
00:13:25,799 --> 00:13:26,799
Lagging behind.

193
00:13:30,879 --> 00:13:31,960
Then let's hurry!

194
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:34,840
Hey, slow down, you two!

195
00:13:35,879 --> 00:13:37,719
Weren't you complaining
that we were too slow?

196
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:01,360
Since you two are alive and well,

197
00:14:01,600 --> 00:14:03,559
take the trash out for me!

198
00:14:34,153 --> 00:14:38,300
"No pause button for life."
